      "description": "Watch Lillestrøm vs Torreense highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 17, 2026. A Tactical Battle in Europe On September 17, 2026, Lillestrøm hosted Torreense in a captivating fixture for the UEFA Europa League . Both sides entered the pitch determined to assert their dominance in a match characterized by physical play and persistent goal-scoring opportunities. The Momentum Shift The visitors broke the deadlock in the 23rd minute when Alejandro Alfaro found the back of the net following a well-placed assist by David Bruno . The momentum remained firmly with Torreense early in the second half, as Manuel Pozo doubled their lead in the 49th minute, assisted by Javi Vazquez . Refusing to surrender, Lillestrøm utilized their bench to inject fresh energy, eventually reaping the rewards in the 79th minute when Thomas Lehne Olsen scored from a Felix Va delivery. Late Drama As the match neared its conclusion, the physical intensity resulted in several bookings. The pivotal moment arrived in the 85th minute, as Nuha Jatta was sent off after picking up his second yellow card of the game. Despite the numerical disadvantage, the scoreline remained unchanged until the referee blew the final whistle, concluding a hard-fought battle."
